= Hu Hanmin Appointed as CEC Chairman

After a quick election due to Sun Yat-sen's death, Hu Hanmin came out on top as the Chairman of the Central Executive Committee. This has strengthened the Rightist faction significantly, as Hu Hanmin now takes the highest position in the Party.

Since Hu Hanmin has two roles at once, Xu Chongzhi has been appointed governor of Guangdong.
